+## Failed session initialization
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the original error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model work follows the failed initialization, and cleanup receives the same session even if initialization only partially allocated resources, so `afterSession` must tolerate absent or partial allocations and cannot assume the turn started or completed ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+The cleanup contract deliberately requires no new lifecycle argument: deployers track their own allocations and release only resources actually acquired. This guarantee is specified by #94; the acceptance test remains red until its implementation lands.
+
